cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite it as below."
title: "Annotation-robustness of single-cell reference mapping for human reprogramming trajectories"
authors:
  - family-names: Kuma
    affiliation: "Graduate School of Frontier Sciences, The University of Tokyo"
    email: morri0723@gmail.com
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"   # TODO
date-released: "2026-06-09"
license: MIT
keywords: [single-cell, trajectory inference, scANVI, reference mapping, reprogramming, out-of-distribution]
abstract: >
  Code and analysis for testing whether cross-protocol single-cell reference
  mapping (scANVI/scArches) is a trustworthy annotation strategy for human
  chemical-reprogramming trajectories, including a geometric out-of-distribution
  score that recovers the cross-protocol mismatch scANVI confidence misses.
